10. REWARD ACCOUNTING

The ledger must be authoritative.

Do not make the dashboard balance the source of truth.

A provider balance should be derived from valid ledger/accounting records.

Ensure:

- double-entry or equivalent accounting integrity where appropriate
- idempotent reward posting
- unique contribution identifiers
- duplicate protection
- reversal support
- correction support
- immutable audit history
- deterministic calculations
- reward rule versioning
- reconciliation

Example conceptual flow:

Validated Contribution #123
        ↓
Reward Rule vX
        ↓
Reward = Y units
        ↓
Ledger Transaction
        ↓
Provider Balance Projection

If the same contribution is submitted twice, it must not produce two rewards.

If a contribution is later invalidated, the system must have a safe correction/reversal mechanism.

Never silently mutate historical accounting records.

