FINAL PRINCIPLE

Do not optimize VIT Network for appearances.

Optimize it for:

CORRECTNESS → INTEGRATION → VERIFIABILITY → SECURITY → ACCOUNTABILITY → RELIABILITY → SCALE

The goal is not to make every dashboard green.

The goal is to make the underlying network actually work.

The most important proof is that a real provider device can contribute useful, verifiable work and that the system can correctly recognize that contribution, validate it, account for it, and record the resulting reward without fabrication or double counting.

Start with the repository and production audit, identify the first broken dependency in the real lifecycle, fix it at the correct architectural boundary, test it, deploy it, verify it, and continue systematically through the ecosystem.This version makes provider recovery + real reward accounting the spine of the whole audit, rather than treating rewards as a disconnected dashboard feature.